bizzi
=====

bizzi includes third-party material listed below. Each item keeps its own licence.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Theming: model, converter and hand-authored themes
(packages/ui/src/lib/theme/)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Chorus (an agentic development environment)
  Licence: Apache License 2.0
  Used: the theme model (semantic tokens, terminal palette, layout tokens per
  light/dark variant), the base16/base24 converter including its YAML
  inline-comment handling, theme validation, and the themes Graphite, Paper,
  Teletype, Abyss and Ink & Bone. Ported to TypeScript modules in bizzi with
  changes (ids and names, bizzi's extra tokens, collected validation failures).
  Chorus's own house palette ("Chorus Default") is not included.

Terax (https://github.com/crynta/terax-ai)
  Licence: Apache License 2.0
  Used: the theme model Chorus descends from, and the themes Tokyo Night,
  Nord, Catppuccin, Gruvbox, Rosé Pine, Tide, Sage, Caffeine and
  Warm Paper & Clay (Terax "claude"), via Chorus. Three light-variant muted
  foregrounds were darkened to meet bizzi's contrast checks.

  The upstream palettes behind those themes are MIT-licensed:
  Tokyo Night (enkia), Nord (Arctic Ice Studio and Sven Greb),
  Catppuccin (Catppuccin), gruvbox (Pavel Pertsev), Rosé Pine (Rosé Pine).

  Apache License 2.0: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

